# Spelunking, "Lands you control enter untapped" (CR 614.1d): Bot1 puts Opulent Palace (a land with its own "This land
# enters tapped", not a Cave: no life) from its hand. Both replacements apply to its entry, and Bot1, its controller, is
# asked which applies first (CR 616.1): the question offers the Palace's own in its words, "This land enters tapped.", and
# Bot1 takes it first; Spelunking's then applies to the land as it now is, and it enters untapped (the ruling). Bot2's own
# Opulent Palace, played on its turn, still enters tapped, unasked: the effect reads "you control", not every land.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Spelunking
Opulent Palace
Lightning Bolt
Lightning Bolt
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Opulent Palace
Plains x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Spelunking.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Opulent Palace)
Bot1.Replace(This land enters tapped)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Opulent Palace.Tapped = false
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Opulent Palace.Play

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot1.Battlefield.Opulent Palace.Tapped = false
Bot2.Battlefield.Opulent Palace.Tapped = true
